      "errorMessage": "<task id=\"ses_f0bbfb459ffejc7I44bHOILDNF\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have completed a thorough investigation. Here is the full map of the server-side AI provider GraphQL surface.\n\n---\n\n# US-102 workspace BYOK — server-side map\n\n## Headline finding\n\nThe workspace BYOK core added by US-102 is **server-internal only**. There is **no GraphQL resolver, DTO, input type, or query/mutation exposing `WorkspaceAiProvider`**. The only provider-config GraphQL surface that exists is the **Admin Panel (instance-level)** resolver, which manages `AI_PROVIDERS` config variables and masks keys with an 8-char prefix. `WorkspaceAiProviderService` is consumed only by `ProviderConfigService`, which is consumed by the registry and (for instance values) by the Admin Panel view. No `twenty-front` code references workspace BYOK yet (US-127 Settings UI is the downstream task).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Entity\n\n**Path:** `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/entities/workspace-ai-provider.entity.ts` (50 lines, full contents)\n\n```ts\n1: import { Column, CreateDateColumn, Entity, PrimaryGeneratedColumn, Unique, UpdateDateColumn } from 'typeorm';\n10: import { WorkspaceRelatedEntity } from 'src/engine/workspace-manager/types/workspace-related-entity';\n14: // One BYOK provider per (workspace, provider key): the key doubles as the\n15: // config key the registry resolves models under ...\n15: @Entity({ name: 'workspaceAiProvider', schema: 'core' })\n16: @Unique('IDX_WORKSPACE_AI_PROVIDER_WORKSPACE_PROVIDER_UNIQUE', ['workspaceId', 'provider'])\n20: export class WorkspaceAiProviderEntity extends WorkspaceRelatedEntity {\n21:   @PrimaryGeneratedColumn('uuid') id: string;\n24:   @Column({ type: 'varchar', nullable: false }) provider: string;\n27:   @Column({ type: 'varchar', nullable: false }) npm: string;\n30:   @Column({ type: 'varchar', nullable: true }) label: string | null;\n33:   @Column({ type: 'text', nullable: true }) encryptedApiKey: string | null;\n36:   @Column({ type: 'varchar', nullable: true }) baseUrl: string | null;\n39:   @Column({ type: 'varchar', nullable: true }) defaultModel: string | null;\n42:   @Column({ type: 'varchar', nullable: true }) fastModel: string | null;\n45:   @CreateDateColumn({ timestamptz }) createdAt: Date;\n48:   @UpdateDateColumn({ timestamptz }) updatedAt: Date;\n49: }\n```\n\nThe API key is stored as **`encryptedApiKey` ciphertext only** — no plaintext column. Unique on `(workspaceId, provider)`. Extends `WorkspaceRelatedEntity` (supplies `workspaceId`).\n\n**Table creation** is via instance upgrade command, not the legacy migration system:\n`packages/twenty-server/src/database/commands/upgrade-version-command/2-39/2-39-instance-command-fast-1790711712877-create-workspace-ai-provider.ts` — `CREATE TABLE \"core\".\"workspaceAiProvider\"` with FK `workspaceId → core.workspace ON DELETE CASCADE` (lines 14-19), plus `down` (lines 22-27).\n\n---\n\n## 2. GraphQL resolvers / DTOs / input types / services for AI provider config\n\n### No resolvers under `ai-models` (or anywhere in `metadata-modules/ai/**`) expose provider config\nAll resolver files in `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/**` are agent/chat/stats related only:\n- `ai-agent/agent.resolver.ts`\n- `ai-chat/resolvers/agent-chat.resolver.ts`, `workspace-setup-chat.resolver.ts`, `agent-chat-subscription.resolver.ts`\n- `ai-agent-execution/resolvers/agent-run.resolver.ts`, `agent-message-part.resolver.ts`\n- `ai-workspace-stats/resolvers/ai-workspace-stats.resolver.ts`\n- `ai-agent-monitor/resolvers/agent-turn.resolver.ts`\n\nThere is **no `*ai*provider*.resolver.ts` under `metadata-modules`**. The only two provider-named resolvers anywhere are `admin-panel/admin-panel-ai-provider.resolver.ts` (instance config) and an unrelated `application/connection-provider/application-connection-provider.resolver.ts`.\n\n### The only provider-config resolver: `admin-panel-ai-provider.resolver.ts`\n**Path:** `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/admin-panel/admin-panel-ai-provider.resolver.ts` (116 lines)\n\nClass `AdminPanelAiProviderResolver` (line 38). Guards: `@AdminResolver()` (line 26), `@UseGuards(WorkspaceAuthGuard, UserAuthGuard, SettingsPermissionGuard(PermissionFlagType.SECURITY))` (lines 33-37), and each field also `@UseGuards(AdminPanelGuard)`. Surface:\n\n| Line | Kind | Field | Args | Returns |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 44-48 | Query | `getCustomAiProviderAccess` | — | `CustomAiProviderAccessDTO` |\n| 50-54 | Query | `getAiProviders` | — | `GraphQLJSON` (masked map) |\n| 56-67 | Mutation | `addAiProvider` | `providerName: String`, `providerConfig: GraphQLJSON` | `Boolean` |\n| 69-76 | Mutation | `removeAiProvider` | `providerName: String` | `Boolean` |\n| 78-82 | Query | `getModelsDevProviders` | — | `[ModelsDevProviderSuggestionDTO]` |\n| 84-90 | Query | `getModelsDevSuggestions` | `providerType: String` | `[ModelsDevModelSuggestionDTO]` |\n| 92-103 | Mutation | `addModelToProvider` | `providerName: String`, `modelConfig: GraphQLJSON` | `Boolean` |\n| 105-115 | Mutation | `removeModelFromProvider` | `providerName: String`, `modelName: String` | `Boolean` |\n\n### Admin Panel model-config surface: `admin-panel.resolver.ts`\n**Path:** `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/admin-panel/admin-panel.resolver.ts`\n- Line 279-327 `@Query(() => AdminAiModelsDTO) getAdminAiModels()` — maps each registry model; per-provider it emits `providerName` (line 311) and `providerLabel` resolved from `getResolvedProvidersForAdmin()` (lines 312-314). The rest of the fields are model metadata (modelId, label, family, costs, flags, `dataResidency`).\n- Lines 329-385: `setAdminAiModelEnabled`, `setAdminAiModelsEnabled`, `setAdminAiModelRecommended`, `setAdminAiModelsRecommended`, `setAdminDefaultAiModel(role, modelId)`.\n\n### DTOs / ObjectTypes\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/admin-panel/dtos/custom-ai-provider-access.dto.ts` — `CustomAiProviderAccessDTO { hasAccess: Boolean; seatCount: Int; seatThreshold: Int }` (lines 6-15).\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/admin-panel/dtos/models-dev-provider-suggestion.dto.ts` — `ModelsDevProviderSuggestion { id, modelCount, npm }` (lines 3-13).\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/admin-panel/dtos/models-dev-model-suggestion.dto.ts` — `ModelsDevModelSuggestion { modelId, name, inputCostPerMillionTokens, outputCostPerMillionTokens, cachedInputCostPerMillionTokens?, cacheCreationCostPerMillionTokens?, contextWindowTokens, maxOutputTokens, modalities, supportsReasoning }` (lines 3-36).\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/client-config/client-config.entity.ts` — `AdminAiModelsDTO` (line 146-158: `models`, `defaultSmartModelId?`, `defaultFastModelId?`) and `AdminAiModelConfig` (fields incl. `providerName?`, `providerLabel?` at lines 132-136).\n\nThere are **no GraphQL `@InputType` classes** for provider config: `providerConfig`/`modelConfig` are untyped `GraphQLJSON` args, validated by Zod schemas (`aiProviderConfigSchema`, `aiProviderModelConfigSchema`) inside the service.\n\n### Services\n- `admin-panel/services/admin-panel-ai-provider.service.ts` (instance custom providers via `AI_PROVIDERS`; detailed in §5).\n- `admin-panel/services/...` companion `admin-panel.module.ts` registers `AdminPanelAiProviderResolver` + `AdminPanelAiProviderService` (lines 94-97).\n- `metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/services/provider-config.service.ts` (resolution — §3).\n- `metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/services/workspace-ai-provider.service.ts` (BYOK CRUD — §3).\n- `metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/services/ai-model-registry.service.ts` (builds registry; `getResolvedProvidersForAdmin` at line 569).\n- `metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/services/models-dev-catalog.service.ts` (suggestions).\n\n---\n\n## 3. `provider-config.service.ts`\n\n**Path:** `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/services/provider-config.service.ts` (166 lines)\n\n### `getResolvedProviders({ includeCustomProviders = true })` — lines 29-46\n```ts\n29: getResolvedProviders({ includeCustomProviders = true }: { includeCustomProviders?: boolean } = {}): AiProvidersConfig {\n32:   const rawCatalog = this.defaultAiCatalogService.getDefaultAiCatalog();\n34:   // Only resolve {{VAR}} templates in the committed catalog — never in user-supplied custom providers\n35:   const catalog = this.resolveTemplates(rawCatalog);\n39:   if (!includeCustomProviders) { return catalog; }\n43:   const custom = this.twentyConfigService.get('AI_PROVIDERS');\n45:   return { ...catalog, ...custom };\n46: }\n```\n- **Returns:** a merged `AiProvidersConfig` (`Record<providerName, AiProviderConfig>`) of committed catalog + instance `AI_PROVIDERS`.\n- **Template resolution** (`{{VAR}}`) applies only to catalog entries (lines 33-35, 118-136), never to custom providers — anti-exfiltration rule. `resolveTemplate` (138-165) reads registered config vars first, then `process.env`.\n- **No masking** — returns real/decrypted `apiKey` values. This is the server-internal registry input.\n\n### `getResolvedProvidersForWorkspace({ workspaceId, includeCustomProviders = true })` — lines 54-88\n```ts\n54: async getResolvedProvidersForWorkspace({ workspaceId, includeCustomProviders = true }): Promise<AiProvidersConfig> {\n61:   const resolvedProviders = this.getResolvedProviders({ includeCustomProviders });\n64:   const workspaceProviders = await this.workspaceAiProviderService.resolveProviders(workspaceId);\n67:   return workspaceProviders.reduce<AiProvidersConfig>((providers, workspaceProvider) => {\n69:     const baseProvider = providers[workspaceProvider.providerName];\n71:     return { ...providers, [workspaceProvider.providerName]: {\n74:         ...baseProvider,\n75:         ...workspaceProvider.providerConfig,\n76:         ...this.buildWorkspaceModelsForProvider({ baseProvider, workspaceProviderModels: [workspaceProvider.defaultModel, workspaceProvider.fastModel] }),\n```\n\n**Resolution order (documented in the comment at lines 48-53): workspace BYOK → instance `AI_PROVIDERS` → committed catalog.** Key behaviors:\n- Workspace entries are merged **last** (override instance/catalog) using the decrypted `providerConfig` (which includes the plaintext `apiKey`).\n- Merged **even when `includeCustomProviders: false`** — deliberate enterprise-entitlement bypass (D-N4): a workspace's own key is billed to its own provider account.\n- Workspace values are **never template-resolved**.\n- `buildWorkspaceModelsForProvider` (94-116): if the base provider has no committed models (e.g. a custom OpenAI-compatible base URL), the workspace's `defaultModel` + `fastModel` are registered as the model list; otherwise the catalog model list is kept.\n- **No masking** — returns decrypted plaintext keys. Only callers are server-internal (`AiModelRegistryService.buildModelRegistry` uses the non-workspace variant) and tests; the workspace variant currently has **no production caller** (grep shows only spec/integration files). This is the \"surface `getResolvedProvidersForWorkspace` in the admin read path\" follow-up noted in the phase report.\n\n### `WorkspaceAiProviderService`\n**Path:** `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/services/workspace-ai-provider.service.ts` (183 lines)\n- `resolveProviders(workspaceId)` (45-53) → `ResolvedWorkspaceAiProvider[]` with **decrypted** `providerConfig` (plaintext `apiKey`), plus `defaultModel`/`fastModel`. Uses `WorkspaceScopedRepository` (workspace isolation).\n- `upsertProvider({...})` (69-125): validates via `aiProviderConfigSchema`, encrypts key with `secretEncryptionService.encryptVersioned(apiKey, { workspaceId })` (lines 113-118); omitted key preserves existing ciphertext; new row without key throws `AiException(INVALID_AGENT_INPUT)`.\n- `removeProvider({workspaceId, provider})` (127-135).\n- `toResolvedProvider` / `decryptApiKeyOrThrow` (137-182): decryption failure surfaces a **safe** error (`API_KEY_NOT_CONFIGURED`, lines 176-181) that does not echo the raw envelope.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Existing GraphQL mutations/queries for AI providers — and is workspace BYOK exposed?\n\n**Yes for instance-level AI providers (Admin Panel only). No for workspace BYOK.**\n\n- Instance provider config: the `AdminPanelAiProviderResolver` (§2) exposes `getAiProviders` / `addAiProvider` / `removeAiProvider` / `addModelToProvider` / `removeModelFromProvider`, gated by `AdminPanelGuard` + `SettingsPermissionGuard(PermissionFlagType.SECURITY)` on an `@AdminResolver()`. This edits the instance-wide `AI_PROVIDERS` config variable (see §5), not per-workspace BYOK.\n- `getAdminAiModels` / `setAdminAiModel*` in `admin-panel.resolver.ts` are likewise Admin-Panel-guarded.\n- **No workspace/member-facing resolver exists for AI provider config.** `WorkspaceAiProviderService` is referenced only by:\n  - `provider-config.service.ts` (line 8, 20, 65)\n  - `ai-models.module.ts` (provider/export, lines 15, 34, 46)\n  - its own specs and the integration spec\n- Grep of `packages/twenty-front/src` for `workspaceAiProvider|WorkspaceAiProvider|upsertProvider|resolveProviders|getResolvedProviders` → **0 matches**. No front-end GraphQL document exists yet.\n- No `@InputType`/`@ObjectType` named `AiProvider`/`AiProviderDTO` exists anywhere in twenty-server.\n\n**Conclusion:** BYOK is currently **server-internal with no resolver**. The phase-14 report confirms this by design (line 37: *\"API keys are never returned by any GraphQL surface in this slice; the only read API added (`resolveProviders`) is server-internal and gated by `WorkspaceScopedRepository` workspace scoping.\"*). The downstream US-127 (M10a-2) is the task that adds the Settings UI / read path.\n\n---\n\n## 5. `AiBillingService` and Admin Panel key masking\n\n### `AiBillingService` — unrelated to provider-key masking\n**Path:** `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-billing/services/ai-billing.service.ts` (213 lines)\n- Class at line 24; dependencies `UsageRecorderService`, `AiModelRegistryService`, `BillingUsageService` (lines 27-31).\n- Methods: `assertAiExecutionAllowed` (33), `calculateCost` (70), `calculateAndBillUsage` (94), `decrementAndCheckAvailableCredits` (127), `billNativeWebSearchUsage` (155), `emitAiTokenUsageEvent` (191).\n- It computes dollar/token cost from model config and records usage/quota. **It contains no API-key handling or masking.** The phase-14 report (lines 34-36) notes there is currently no per-workspace BYOK billing path and flags M10d as the follow-up.\n\n### Admin Panel masking\nThere is **no `maskedApiKey` field** anywhere in the repo (grep across the whole repo → 0 matches). Masking is inline in:\n\n**Path:** `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/admin-panel/services/admin-panel-ai-provider.service.ts` → `getMaskedProviders()` (lines 53-85):\n```ts\n53: getMaskedProviders(): Record<string, unknown> {\n54:   const providers = this.aiModelRegistryService.getResolvedProvidersForAdmin();\n55:   const catalogNames = this.aiModelRegistryService.getCatalogProviderNames();\n56:   const rawCatalog = this.defaultAiCatalogService.getDefaultAiCatalog();\n60:   for (const [key, config] of Object.entries(providers)) {\n61:     const isCatalog = catalogNames.has(key);\n62:     const rawConfig = isCatalog ? rawCatalog[key] : undefined;\n63:     const apiKeyConfigVariable = rawConfig ? extractConfigVariableName(rawConfig.apiKey) : undefined;\n67:     masked[key] = {\n68:       npm: config.npm,\n69:       label: config.label ?? key,\n70:       source: isCatalog ? 'catalog' : 'custom',\n...   baseUrl / region / dataResidency spread conditionally\n76:       ...(config.apiKey && {\n77:         apiKey: `${config.apiKey.substring(0, 8)}...`,   // <-- 8-char prefix masking\n78:       }),\n79:       ...(apiKeyConfigVariable && { apiKeyConfigVariable }),\n80:       hasAccessKey: !!(config.accessKeyId && config.secretAccessKey),\n81:     };\n82:   }\n83:   return masked;\n84: }\n```\n- Only an **8-character prefix + `...`** of the API key is returned; AWS-style creds are reduced to the boolean `hasAccessKey`. For catalog providers it also exposes the config **variable name** (`apiKeyConfigVariable`), never the value.\n- The masked view is fed by the **instance** `getResolvedProvidersForAdmin()` (line 55) → `ProviderConfigService.getResolvedProviders()` (`ai-model-registry.service.ts:569-571`). It does **not** touch workspace BYOK.\n- Unmasked key handling is confined to server-internal `provider-config.service.ts` / `workspace-ai-provider.service.ts` (decrypt in `decryptApiKeyOrThrow`), which never reach GraphQL responses.\n\n### Supporting config schema/type\n- `ai-provider-config.schema.ts` (lines 8-21): `npm` (enum `AI_SDK_PACKAGES`), optional `name`, `label`, `authType`, `apiKey`, `baseUrl`, `region`, `dataResidency`, `accessKeyId`, `secretAccessKey`, `sessionToken`, `models[]`.\n- `ai-provider-config.type.ts`: `AiProviderConfig = Omit<z.infer<...>, 'models'> & { models?: AiProviderModelConfig[] }`.\n- `ai-provider-model-config.schema.ts` (lines 7-35): model name/label/kind/costs/context/modalities.\n- `ai-models.module.ts`: `TypeOrmModule.forFeature([WorkspaceAiProviderEntity])` (line 23), `WorkspaceAiProviderService` + `provideWorkspaceScopedRepository(...)` (34-35), exported (46).\n\n---\n\n## Summary table\n\n| Concern | Exposed via GraphQL? | Where |\n|---|---|---|\n| Workspace BYOK CRUD (`upsertProvider`/`removeProvider`/`resolveProviders`) | **No** | `metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/services/workspace-ai-provider.service.ts` (server-internal) |\n| Workspace-aware resolution `getResolvedProvidersForWorkspace` | **No** | `provider-config.service.ts:54-88` |\n| Instance AI providers (masked list + add/remove) | Yes, Admin Panel | `admin-panel-ai-provider.resolver.ts` |\n| Instance models admin (enable/recommend/default + list) | Yes, Admin Panel | `admin-panel.resolver.ts:279-385` |\n| Key masking | Admin Panel only | `admin-panel-ai-provider.service.ts:76-78` (`substring(0,8)`) |\n| `AiBillingService` | Not a key surface | `ai-billing/services/ai-billing.service.ts` |\n\nNo files were modified.\n</task_result>\n</task>",
