      "result": "<task id=\"ses_f0bbfb48cffexX05PFeW7y4xc1\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have gathered everything needed. Here is the complete map.\n\n---\n\n# AI Provider Settings UI + GraphQL Map (packages/twenty-front)\n\n## Key finding up front\n\nThere are **two distinct AI \"surfaces\"** in the frontend:\n\n1. **Workspace settings → \"Syna\"** (`/settings/ai`) — workspace-level AI config (models, agents, skills, tools, usage, audit). This is *not* where AI providers are managed. It reads the already-resolved model catalog from client config.\n2. **Admin Panel → AI tab** (`/settings/admin-panel#ai`) — the instance-level **AI providers** management UI. This is the real \"AI providers page\", built on a separate GraphQL schema/client and a separate permission gate.\n\nTerms you asked to search (`adminAiProvider`, `resolveProviders`, `upsertProvider`) **do not exist anywhere in the frontend**. `resolveProviders`/`upsertProvider` are server-only service methods (`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/ai/ai-models/services/workspace-ai-provider.service.ts:45,69`). The frontend equivalent is the `getAiProviders` query + `addAiProvider`/`removeAiProvider` mutations.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Settings AI pages and modules\n\n### A. `packages/twenty-front/src/pages/settings/ai/` (workspace \"Syna\" pages)\n\nTop-level pages:\n- `SettingsAI.tsx` — main Syna page. Renders `SettingsPageLayout` titled `Syna` (line 87), a hero card, and a `SettingsTabBar` with tabs Overview / Models / Skills / Tools / Usage / Audit (lines 40-71, 141-146). No providers UI.\n- `SettingsAgentForm.tsx` — create/edit agent (`mode=\"create\" | \"edit\"`), routed at `AiNewAgent` / `AiAgentDetail`.\n- `SettingsAgentTurnDetail.tsx` — agent turn detail.\n- `SettingsAiPrompts.tsx` — system prompt viewer.\n- `SettingsAiUsageUserDetail.tsx` — per-user AI usage.\n- `SettingsSkillForm.tsx` — create/edit skill.\n- `SettingsToolDetail.tsx` — tool detail.\n\nComponents (`pages/settings/ai/components/`): `SettingsAgentSkillsTab.tsx`, `SettingsAiAuditTab.tsx` (masked credential display — see §2), `SettingsAiOverviewTab.tsx`, `SettingsAgentToolsTab.tsx`, `SettingsAgentSkillsTable.tsx`, `SettingsAgentDetailSkeletonLoader.tsx`, `SettingsSkillInactiveMenuDropDown.tsx`, `SettingsAiModelsTab.tsx`, `SettingsSkillTableRow.tsx`, `SettingsAgentResponseFormat.tsx`, `SettingsAgentRoleTab.tsx`, `SettingsToolIcon.tsx`, `SettingsToolTableRow.tsx`, `SettingsToolParameterTable.tsx`, `SettingsAgentDeleteConfirmationModal.tsx`, `SettingsAgentLogsTab.tsx`, `SettingsAgentEvalsTab.tsx`, `SettingsAgentToolsTable.tsx`, `SettingsAgentSettingsTab.tsx`, `SettingsAiUsageTab.tsx`.\n\nConstants / hooks / types / utils / validation:\n- `constants/SettingsAiTabs.ts` (tab ids), `constants/SettingsAgentDetailTabs.ts`, `constants/SettingsSkillTableMetadata.ts`.\n- `hooks/useSettingsAgentToolsTable.ts`, `useCreateTool.ts`, `useSettingsAgentFormState.ts`, `useSettingsAiModelsActions.ts` (workspace `smartModel`/`fastModel` via `UpdateWorkspaceDocument`).\n- `graphql/queries/findManyApplicationsForToolTable.ts`, `graphql/queries/findManyMarketplaceAppsForToolTable.ts`.\n- `types/SettingsAgentTool*.ts`; `utils/getToolLink.ts`, `getToolApplicationId.ts`, and `getAiProviderCredentialStatuses.ts` (credential masking); `validation-schemas/settingsAiAgentFormSchema.ts`.\n\n### B. `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/ai/` (shared workspace AI components)\n\n- `components/SettingsAiModelHoverCard.tsx` — model hover detail.\n- `components/SettingsAiModelsTable.tsx` — generic model table (checkbox toggle, optional provider column, optional remove). Used by both the workspace Models tab and the admin AI pages.\n- `types/AiModelSummary.ts` — common model shape (`modelId`, `label`, `providerName`, `providerLabel`, …).\n- `utils/getModelIcon.ts`, `utils/getDataResidencyDisplay.ts`.\n\n### C. `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ai/` (chat/agent product module, NOT provider settings)\n\n100 files under `components/`, plus `constants/`, `contexts/`, `dictation/`, `graphql/`, `hooks/`, `states/`, `types/`, `utils/`. This is the in-app AI chat/agent experience (threads, streaming, composer, tool calls). No provider-settings code. The resolved model catalog it consumes lives at `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/client-config/states/aiModelsState.ts` (populated by `useClientConfig`), and availability is computed in `modules/ai/hooks/useWorkspaceAiModelAvailability.ts`.\n\n### D. Admin Panel AI providers (the page you're actually after)\n\nComponents — `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/admin-panel/ai/components/`:\n- `SettingsAdminAI.tsx` — the admin AI tab content. Sections: **Providers** (catalog, `showAddButton={false}`, lines 194-204), **Custom Providers** (lines 206-229, with enterprise gate), **Default Models** (231-274), **Recommended Models** (276-315), **Chats** (317-330), **AI Usage by Workspace** (332-394). Uses the admin Apollo client.\n- `SettingsAdminAiProviderListCard.tsx` — renders provider rows via `SettingsListCard`; each row links to `AdminPanelAiProviderDetail` and shows a `Status` badge \"Configured\" / \"No credentials\" (lines 26-49, 78-89). Description is built from `region` / `baseUrl` / `authType` only.\n- `ModelsDevProviderLogo.tsx`.\n\nPages — `packages/twenty-front/src/pages/settings/admin-panel/`:\n- `SettingsAdminAiProviderDetail.tsx` — provider detail. Builds `providerInfoItems` (lines 205-295): Name, SDK, **API Key**, Base URL, Region, Credentials, Data Residency. API key display logic (lines 227-254): if `apiKeyConfigVariable` exists it links to the config-variable page showing `provider.apiKey` or \"Configure\"; otherwise renders `provider.apiKey` directly. Model list with per-provider toggle + remove (custom only); danger zone to remove provider.\n- `SettingsAdminNewAiProvider.tsx` — create custom provider form (models.dev catalog select, or custom mode): npm package, label, API key (`type=\"password\"`), base URL, data residency, AWS Bedrock region/access key/secret. Gated by `hasCustomAiProviderAccess`.\n- `SettingsAdminNewAiModel.tsx` — add a model to a custom provider (models.dev suggestions, modalities, costs, context windows).\n\nSupporting module — `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/admin-panel/ai/`:\n- `constants/AiAdminPath.ts` — `AI_ADMIN_PATH = /settings/admin-panel#ai` (via `getSettingsPath(AdminPanel, …, 'ai')`).\n- `constants/AiProviderSource.ts`, `DataResidencyConfig.ts`, `DataResidencyOptions.ts`, `ModelIconConfig.ts`, `ProviderConfig.ts`.\n- `hooks/useCustomAiProviderAccess.ts` — enterprise seat-threshold gate (see §4/§5).\n- `types/AiProviderAuthType.ts` (`'key' | 'credentials' | 'role'`), `types/AiProviderSource.ts` (`'catalog' | 'custom'`), `types/AiProviderItem.ts`, `types/RawAiProviderConfig.ts` (`Omit<AiProviderItem,'id'>`), `types/GetAiProvidersResult.ts`, `types/GetCustomAiProviderAccessResult.ts`.\n- `utils/parseProviderItems.ts` (converts the `Record<id, config>` into `AiProviderItem[]`), `isKnownProviderId.ts`, `getProviderIcon.ts`, `getModelsDevLogoIcon.tsx`, `isModelIconKey.ts`.\n- `graphql/` — see §3.\n\n### How instance providers are displayed/masked\n\n- The backend `getAiProviders` query returns `getMaskedProviders()` (`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/admin-panel/services/admin-panel-ai-provider.service.ts:53-85`). It returns a `Record<string, RawAiProviderConfig>`, and deliberately:\n  - **masks `apiKey` to `\"<first 8 chars>...\"`** (lines 76-78),\n  - never returns `accessKeyId`/`secretAccessKey`; instead exposes a boolean `hasAccessKey` (line 80),\n  - exposes `apiKeyConfigVariable` (the env var name) for catalog providers instead of the key.\n- Frontend types mirror this: `RawAiProviderConfig`/`AiProviderItem` include `apiKey?`, `apiKeyConfigVariable?`, `hasAccessKey?` (`modules/settings/admin-panel/ai/types/AiProviderItem.ts:20-24`). `SettingsAdminAiProviderListCard` never prints the key — only \"API key configured\" / \"IAM credentials\" (`SettingsAdminAiProviderListCard.tsx:37-43`). `SettingsAdminAiProviderDetail` renders the masked `provider.apiKey` or a link to configure (`SettingsAdminAiProviderDetail.tsx:227-254`).\n- The workspace **Audit tab** additionally renders every credential as a fixed mask `'••••••••'` (`pages/settings/ai/utils/getAiProviderCredentialStatuses.ts:7` and usage at `pages/settings/ai/components/SettingsAiAuditTab.tsx:43,105,118-119`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. `SettingsPath` enum and how a \"Settings → Syna → Providers\" page is registered\n\n**Definition:** `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/SettingsPath.ts`\n- Existing AI workspace entries: `AI = 'ai'` (line 40), `AiUsageUserDetail` (41), `AiPrompts` (42), `AiNewAgent` (43), `AiAgentDetail` (44), `AiAgentTurnDetail` (45), `AiNewSkill` (46), `AiSkillDetail` (47), `AiToolDetail` (48).\n- Existing admin AI entries: `AdminPanelNewAiProvider = 'admin-panel/ai/new-provider'` (84), `AdminPanelAiProviderDetail = 'admin-panel/ai/providers/:providerName'` (85), `AdminPanelNewAiModel` (86).\n- Exported through `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/index.ts:315`.\n- Path builder: `packages/twenty-shared/src/utils/navigation/getSettingsPath.ts` (params, query, hash).\n\n**The settings navigation file + AI group:** `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/hooks/useSettingsNavigationItems.tsx`\n- The AI settings group is the workspace item **`Syna`** at lines **171-175**:\n  ```\n  label: t`Syna`, path: SettingsPath.AI, Icon: IconSparkles,\n  isHidden: !permissionMap[PermissionFlagType.AI_SETTINGS]\n  ```\n- Items support `subItems` (`SettingsNavigationItem`, lines 47-58). Rendered by `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/components/SettingsNavigationDrawerItems.tsx` (subitem rendering at lines 22-81; item type import lines 3-7).\n\n**Router:** `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/app/components/SettingsRoutes.tsx`\n- Lazy imports at lines 253-385 and 591-613.\n- Workspace AI group (permission `AI_SETTINGS`) at lines **808-849**: `AI`, `AiPrompts`, `AiNewAgent`, `AiAgentDetail`, `AiAgentTurnDetail`, `AiNewSkill`, `AiSkillDetail`, `AiUsageUserDetail`, `AiToolDetail`, `LogicFunctionDetail`.\n- Admin Panel routes gated by `isAdminPageEnabled` at lines **1094-1164** (AI provider routes at 1131-1142).\n- Route objects are assembled in `createSettingsRouteObjects` (1186-1193) and mounted by `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/app/routing/utils/createWorkspaceRouteObjects.tsx:88-94`.\n\n**To register a new `Settings → Syna → Providers` page you would:**\n1. Add an enum value in `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/SettingsPath.ts` (e.g. `AiProviders = 'ai/providers'`) — then rebuild `twenty-shared` (`npx nx build twenty-shared`) per the repo gotcha.\n2. Add a lazy import + `<Route path={SettingsPath.AiProviders} …/>` inside the `PermissionFlagType.AI_SETTINGS` group in `SettingsRoutes.tsx` (lines 808-849).\n3. Add a `subItems` entry under the `Syna` item in `useSettingsNavigationItems.tsx` (line 171) with its own `isHidden` guard.\n4. Optionally add a title prefix in `packages/twenty-front/src/utils/title-utils.ts` (`SettingsPathPrefixes`, lines 4-16). Note: there is currently **no** `AI`/`Syna` title prefix, so Syna pages fall through to the default `'A2E Suite'` (line 65).\n\nFor an **admin-panel** AI provider page, follow the existing pattern: add enum in the `AdminPanel*` block, lazy import + route inside the `isAdminPageEnabled` block, and register in the admin tabs (`constants/SettingsAdminTabs.ts`) / `SettingsAdminTabContent.tsx`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. GraphQL operations for AI providers\n\n### Hand-written documents (frontend)\nQueries — `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/admin-panel/ai/graphql/queries/`:\n- `getAiProviders.ts:3-7` — `query GetAiProviders { getAiProviders }` (raw JSON record).\n- `getCustomAiProviderAccess.ts:3-11` — `{ hasAccess, seatCount, seatThreshold }`.\n- `getAdminAiModels.ts:3-28` — model catalog + default smart/fast ids.\n- `getAdminAiUsageByWorkspace.ts:3-17`.\n- `getModelsDevProviders.ts`, `getModelsDevSuggestions.ts`.\n\nMutations — `.../ai/graphql/mutations/`:\n- `addAiProvider.ts:3-7` — `addAiProvider(providerName, providerConfig: JSON)`.\n- `removeAiProvider.ts:3-7`.\n- `addModelToProvider.ts`, `removeModelFromProvider.ts`.\n- `setAdminAiModelEnabled.ts`, `setAdminAiModelRecommended.ts`, `setAdminAiModelsEnabled.ts`, `setAdminAiModelsRecommended.ts`, `setAdminDefaultAiModel.ts`.\n\n### Generated code location\n- **`packages/twenty-front/src/generated-admin/graphql.ts`** — this is the generated file for all admin-panel AI operations. Relevant lines:\n  - Types: `AdminAiModelConfig` (21), `AdminAiModels` (42), `CustomAiProviderAccessDto` (383).\n  - Mutation fields (520-536): `addAiProvider`, `addModelToProvider`, `removeAiProvider`, `removeModelFromProvider`, `setAdminAiModel*`.\n  - Query fields (705-718): `getAdminAiModels`, `getAdminAiUsageByWorkspace`, `getAiProviders`, `getCustomAiProviderAccess`, `getModelsDevProviders`, `getModelsDevSuggestions`.\n  - Generated documents (1518-1532): `AddAiProviderDocument`, `RemoveAiProviderDocument`, `GetAiProvidersDocument`, `GetCustomAiProviderAccessDocument`, etc.\n- Codegen config: `packages/twenty-front/codegen-admin.cjs` — schema is `<server>/admin-panel` (line 2-4), documents glob `./src/modules/settings/admin-panel/**/graphql/**/*.{ts,tsx}` (line 6), output `./src/generated-admin/graphql.ts` (line 15). Note the admin schema is **separate**; the workspace `generated-metadata/graphql.ts` and `generated/graphql.ts` contain **no** `AiProvider` symbols (verified).\n- Workspace-side generated operations (agents, skills, `UpdateWorkspace`, model preview) live in `packages/twenty-front/src/generated-metadata/graphql.ts`.\n\n### Consumers / hooks\n- `useCustomAiProviderAccess.ts` uses `GET_CUSTOM_AI_PROVIDER_ACCESS`.\n- `SettingsAdminAI.tsx` uses `GET_AI_PROVIDERS`, `GET_ADMIN_AI_MODELS`, `GET_ADMIN_AI_USAGE_BY_WORKSPACE` and the set-model mutations with `client: apolloAdminClient` (lines 81-117).\n- Admin client: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/admin-panel/apollo/hooks/useApolloAdminClient.ts` (context provider `modules/settings/admin-panel/apollo/components/ApolloAdminProvider.tsx`).\n- Server counterparts: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/admin-panel/admin-panel-ai-provider.resolver.ts` (queries/mutations lines 44-115) and service `admin-panel-ai-provider.service.ts`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Representative Linaria + theme-token + Lingui component\n\nGood, compact examples to match style:\n\n- **`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/ai/components/SettingsAiModelsTable.tsx`** — the canonical pattern: `import { styled } from '@linaria/react'` (3), `import { Trans } from '@lingui/react/macro'` (5), `import { ThemeContext, themeCssVariables } from 'twenty-ui/theme-constants'` (10), styled blocks using `${themeCssVariables.spacing[2]}` / `${themeCssVariables.font.color.light}` (lines 26-48), and JSX using `<Trans>Name</Trans>` (105).\n- Smaller admin example: **`packages/twenty-front/src/pages/settings/admin-panel/SettingsAdminNewAiModel.tsx`** lines 3-15, 33-57 — `styled.div` with `themeCssVariables.spacing`, `t` from `@lingui/core/macro`, `Trans` from `@lingui/react/macro`.\n- Layout/typography conventions: `H2Title` + `Section` + `SettingsPageLayout` + `SettingsPageContainer` (see `SettingsAdminAI.tsx:192-204` and `SettingsAiModelsTab.tsx:113-152`).\n- List/card convention for provider rows: `SettingsAdminAiProviderListCard.tsx` (`styled` + `SettingsListCard` + `t`).\n\nNote the two Lingui import styles in use: direct `t` from `@lingui/core/macro` (most files) and `useLingui()` destructured `t` (e.g. `SettingsAdminNewAiProvider.tsx:50`). Match the neighboring file.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Admin-only gating and router wiring\n\n### Workspace permission gating\n- Route-level: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/components/SettingsProtectedRouteWrapper.tsx` — wraps routes with `settingsPermission` (a `PermissionFlagType`) and optional `requiredFeatureFlag`; on failure redirects to `SettingsPath.ProfilePage` (or shows `WorkspaceRouteUnavailable` in the side panel) (lines 27-51).\n- Hook: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/roles/hooks/useHasPermissionFlag.ts` — checks `currentUserWorkspace.permissionFlags` (27-28).\n- Map: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/roles/hooks/usePermissionFlagMap.ts` — `Record<PermissionFlagType, boolean>` used by the nav.\n- The Syna group is gated by `PermissionFlagType.AI_SETTINGS` both in the nav (`useSettingsNavigationItems.tsx:174`) and routes (`SettingsRoutes.tsx:808-813`).\n\n### Admin Panel gating\n- Enablement flag: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/app/components/WorkspaceApp.tsx:12-14`:\n  `isAdminPageEnabled = currentUser?.canImpersonate || currentUser?.canAccessFullAdminPanel`.\n- Passed into the router via `useCreateWorkspaceAppRouter` (`modules/app/hooks/useCreateWorkspaceAppRouter.tsx:104-113,278-287`) → `createWorkspaceRouteObjects` (`.../createWorkspaceRouteObjects.tsx:88-94`) → `createSettingsRouteObjects` → the `{isAdminPageEnabled && (…)}` block in `SettingsRoutes.tsx:1094-1164`.\n- Nav: Admin Panel item hidden unless `isAdminEnabled` (`useSettingsNavigationItems.tsx:68-70, 188-194`).\n- Admin tabs: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/admin-panel/hooks/useSettingsAdminTabs.ts:19-41` — each tab `disabled: !canAccessFullAdminPanel` (AI tab at 37-41). Tab content switch: `modules/settings/admin-panel/components/SettingsAdminTabContent.tsx:20-39` (AI → `SettingsAdminAI`).\n- Server-side: the admin AI resolver is guarded by `@AdminResolver()`, `@UseGuards(WorkspaceAuthGuard, UserAuthGuard, SettingsPermissionGuard(PermissionFlagType.SECURITY))`, and each field additionally `@UseGuards(AdminPanelGuard)` (`admin-panel-ai-provider.resolver.ts:26-44`). The custom-provider creation paths additionally check the enterprise seat threshold (`admin-panel-ai-provider.service.ts:40-51`), surfaced in the UI by `useCustomAiProviderAccess` and `SettingsEnterpriseFeatureGateCard` (`SettingsAdminAI.tsx:222-228`).\n\n### Notes for adding a new page\n- Repo gotcha: after editing `packages/twenty-shared` (`SettingsPath`), run `npx nx build twenty-shared --skip-nx-cache` before trusting dependent typechecks.\n- Admin-panel GraphQL documents are picked up automatically by `codegen-admin.cjs` (glob on `src/modules/settings/admin-panel/**/graphql/**/*.ts`), so a new provider mutation/query should live under that tree to be generated into `src/generated-admin/graphql.ts`.\n\n---\n\nNo files were modified.\n</task_result>\n</task>"
